{
	"info": {
		"name": "16 · Task completions",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"description": "Task check-off — a red-teamer marking a scenario's tasks done inside a conversation, plus the per-group roll-up.\n\n**Flow.** A) build the chain admin-side — group → **approve** → evaluation → scenario → task → model → assign → conversation group (posted to the scenario, yielding one conversation); B) **PUT** to check the task off (idempotent), list the conversation's completions, read the group roll-up, **DELETE** to uncheck, confirm it's gone; C) negatives — a `task_id` outside the scenario is **404**, a `viewer` (no `conversations:update`) is **403**, no-token is **401**.\n\n**Auth model.** Per-request: `{{admin_token}}` (holds `conversations:*` and owns the conversation) drives the flow, `{{viewer_token}}` for the 403, `noauth` for the 401. Self-contained — no `00-bootstrap`, no manual token, no SSE (the conversation is created directly, not via the streaming message endpoint).\n\n**Gotcha.** A fresh group is `pending_approval`; evaluations 409 until it's approved — folder A approves before creating the evaluation. Check-off requires the caller to **own** the conversation and the `task_id` to belong to its scenario.\n\n**Leftovers.** The evaluation group leaks (no group DELETE; `run_suffix` keeps it unique); the conversation, evaluation (+scenario/task/assignment) and model are deleted in Teardown.\n\n**Verified:** 28/28 checks green end-to-end against a live stack (`make up` + `make seedlocal`)."
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "noauth"
	},
